  "question": {
    "text": "If the function $f(x)=\\left(\\frac{1}{x}\\right)^{2 x} ; x>0$ attains the maximum value at $x=\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{e}}$ then :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "CmLcB",
      "text": "$\\mathrm{e}^\\pi < \\pi^{\\mathrm{e}}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GrAZm",
      "text": "$\\mathrm{e}^\\pi>\\pi^{\\mathrm{e}}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "AqLYa",
      "text": "$(2 e)^\\pi>\\pi^{(2 e)}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "zlpw9",
      "text": "$\\mathrm{e}^{2 \\pi} < (2 \\pi)^{\\mathrm{e}}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let $y=\\left(\\frac{1}{x}\\right)^{2 x}$\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\ell \\text { ny }=2 x \\ell n\\left(\\frac{1}{x}\\right) \\\\\n& \\ell \\text { ny }=-2 x \\ell \\ln x \\\\\n& \\frac{1}{y} \\frac{d y}{d x}=-2(1+\\ell n x)\n\\end{aligned}$\nfor $\\mathrm{x}>\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{e}} \\mathrm{f}^{\\mathrm{n}}$ is decreasing\n$\\text {so, } \\mathrm{e} < \\pi$\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\left(\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{e}}\\right)^{2 \\mathrm{e}}>\\left(\\frac{1}{\\pi}\\right)^{2 \\pi} \\\\\n& \\mathrm{e}^\\pi>\\pi^{\\mathrm{e}}\n\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
